From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Garcia Brisa <d.garciabrisa@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:35:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] launcher: choose a CEF remote debugging port per launch

CEF serves its DevTools endpoint on one loopback port, read once when
the native layer initializes CEF. The port is either fixed in the
build's chromiumFlags or scanned from 9222 in dev builds, and an app
cannot set ELECTROBUN_CEF_REMOTE_DEBUGGING_PORT itself: its Worker
starts after the main thread has entered the native event loop, and
Bun's process.env does not reach the C runtime's getenv anyway. A fixed
port collides with a second instance or another app, and is known in
advance to anything that wants to squat on it.

chromiumFlags["remote-debugging-port"] = "launch" now asks the launcher
to reserve a free loopback port before it loads the native core, set
it in the process environment through setenv (SetEnvironmentVariableW
on Windows), and in process.env for the app's Worker. The native layer
then takes the environment path it already has. A port already set in
the environment wins, and when the launcher cannot set one, CEF reads
"launch" as an invalid port and keeps remote debugging off, as before.
